:\n        if not args:\n            args = (app_ctx._get_current_object(),)\n        elif not isinstance(args[0], AppContext):\npyproject.toml:22:requires-python = \">=3.10\"\n# Teardown cleanup errors\n\n## Goal\n\nRun every Flask teardown callback and signal before surfacing teardown errors.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- TBD\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] TBD\n\n## Notes\n\n- Keep `prd.md` focused on requirements, constraints, and acceptance criteria.\n- Lightweight tasks can remain PRD-only.\n- For complex tasks, add `design.md` for technical design and `implement.md` for execution planning before `task.py start`.\n{\n  \"id\": \"teardown-cleanup-errors\",\n  \"name\": \"teardown-cleanup-errors\",\n  \"title\": \"Teardown cleanup errors\",\n  \"description\": \"Run every Flask teardown callback and signal before surfacing teardown errors.\",\n  \"status\": \"planning\",\n  \"dev_type\": null,\n  \"scope\": null,\n  \"package\": null,\n  \"priority\": \"P2\",\n  \"creator\": \"benchmark\",\n  \"assignee\": \"benchmark\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-20\",\n  \"completedAt\": null,\n  \"branch\": null,\n  \"base_branch\": \"main\",\n  \"worktree_path\": null,\n  \"commit\": null,\n  \"pr_url\": null,\n  \"subtasks\": [],\n  \"children\": [],\n  \"parent\": null,\n  \"relatedFiles\": [],\n  \"notes\": \"\",\n  \"meta\": {}\n}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
